<h3>3. Right of Withdrawal and Return</h3>
<p><strong><u>Exercise of the Right of Withdrawal shall apply only where one of the parties acts for the purpose of engaging in commercial activity; in transactions between two natural persons who do not have that capacity, Consumer Legislation and the withdrawal/return provisions connected therewith shall not apply.</u></strong></p>

<p><strong><u>The Buyer accepts, declares and undertakes that on sutore.com there are sellers who are not merchants, tradespeople, suppliers or commercial sellers and who sell only a product belonging to them without a professional/commercial purpose; that sellers/providers who do not act for a professional/commercial purpose</u></strong><strong> <u>do not fall within the scope of the <a href="https://www.mevzuat.gov.tr/MevzuatMetin/1.5.6502.pdf">Law No. 6502 on the Protection of Consumers</a></u> <u>and that therefore it cannot exercise the right of withdrawal against such sellers.</u></strong></p>

<p>The Buyer (Member) may exercise the right of withdrawal and return the goods/service within 14 (fourteen) days from delivery of the goods or service to it, without stating any reason. The Buyer Member shall deliver the notice of exercise of the right of withdrawal to the Seller in the manner specified on sutore.com. The Seller is obliged to refund the Goods/Service price within 14 (fourteen) days from receipt of the Buyer's withdrawal declaration. Where there are justified reasons why the service cannot be taken back, the Seller may supply the Buyer with Goods/Service of equal quality and price before the performance period under the Agreement expires. If the Seller considers that performance of the goods/service has become impossible, it shall notify the Buyer of this before the performance period of the Agreement expires. In that case the Seller shall refund the paid price and any documents to the Buyer within 14 (fourteen) days. If a product sought to be returned under the right of withdrawal is not sent by the contracted courier company where so stated in this Form, the Buyer shall be responsible for the return shipping cost.</p>

<p>The right of withdrawal may not be exercised in the following cases: a) Contracts concerning goods or services whose price varies depending on fluctuations in financial markets and which are not under the seller's control (products in the jewellery, gold and silver categories) b) Contracts for the delivery of goods prepared in accordance with the consumer's requests or clearly for the consumer's personal needs, which by their nature are not suitable for return, are liable to rapidly deteriorate, or may pass their expiry date c) Contracts for the delivery of goods whose protective elements such as packaging, tape, seal or wrapping have been opened after delivery, where return is not suitable from a health and hygiene perspective d) Contracts concerning goods which after delivery are mixed with other products and cannot by their nature be separated e) Contracts concerning books, sound or image recordings, software programmes and computer consumables presented on a tangible medium, provided that the protective elements such as packaging, tape, seal or wrapping have been opened by the consumer f) Contracts for the delivery of periodicals such as newspapers and magazines, other than those provided under a subscription agreement g) Contracts concerning accommodation, carriage of goods, car rental, supply of food and drink, and leisure activities for entertainment or recreation purposes that must be performed on a specific date or within a specific period h) Contracts for the performance of betting and lottery services ı) Contracts for services whose performance has begun with the consumer's approval before the withdrawal period expires i) Contracts for services performed instantly in electronic form and intangible goods delivered instantly to the consumer; and where the Goods/Service subject to the Agreement consist of Goods/Service types excluded from the scope of application of the Distance Contracts Regulation (foodstuffs, beverages or other daily consumables delivered to the buyer's residence by the seller's regular deliveries, and services in areas such as travel, accommodation, catering and entertainment), the right of withdrawal cannot be exercised because the provisions of the Distance Contracts Regulation cannot be applied to the legal relationship between the Buyer and the Seller. The cancellation and return conditions of such Goods/Services offered for sale in the holiday category are subject to the Seller's practices and rules.</p>

<h3>4. Resolution of Disputes</h3>

<p>Under the <a href="https://www.mevzuat.gov.tr/MevzuatMetin/1.5.6502.pdf">Law No. 6502 on the Protection of Consumers and the Distance Contracts Regulation</a>, liability relating to the sold goods or service belongs to the seller itself. Nevertheless, if the Buyer submits complaints relating to purchased goods and services to sutore Elektronik Hizmetler ve Ticaret Anonim Şirketi in its capacity as Intermediary Service Provider, either directly or via sutore.com, the Company shall provide all possible support for resolution of the problem.</p>

<p>In disputes arising from the application of this Agreement; up to the value announced by the Ministry of Customs and Trade, the Consumer Arbitration Committees at the place where the Buyer purchased the goods or where the Buyer's domicile is located shall have jurisdiction; for disputes exceeding that value, the Consumer Courts at the place where the Buyer's or the Seller's domicile is located shall have jurisdiction.</p>

